{"kind":"request","text":"Rule on registration admission before O4 opens its dedicated Worker\n\nThe independent DCR approval d2bfa044 accepts the completed bounded expiry/reclamation and Native grant-retention change, including its explicit failed-gate record. It also names two remaining capacity limits. Anonymous callers can fill 1,000 one-hour registration slots repeatedly and sustain denial cheaply. An authorized member can consent to 1,000 clients and protect them for up to 30 days, with each consent recorded in Native.\n\nBefore O4 opens POST /oauth/register on its new dedicated Worker, please record either the edge admission/rate-limit policy that bounds the anonymous refill, or explicit acceptance of that named residual risk for the bounded witness. Also record how the witness treats the authorized-member protection limit. No existing live Worker changes register or opens hosted MCP, and builder performs no deployment. The source landing alone does not open O4 or satisfy its acceptance. The planner names and deploys the dedicated Worker under the O4 sequence.\n\nThis asks for a concrete deployment policy, not another full suite or a claim that reclamation supplies rate limiting. DCR's existing record states the anonymous and protected-capacity limits. The checker found no blocking source issue.","body":{"conditions":"Before O4 registration opens, planner records bounded edge admission or names acceptance of anonymous sustained refill and authorized-member protected-capacity limits on the dedicated witness Worker.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}